.TH CLADENC-STATUS 1 "" cladenc "cladenc"
.SH NAME
cladenc\-status \- print the state so far of a directed evolution that has not ended, without changing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBcladenc status\fP
    [\fB\-\-help\fP]
    [\fB\-\-json\fP]
    \fB\-\-outputs\-dir\fP <DIR>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcladenc status\fP is for a directed evolution that has not ended, whether
the directed evolution is still going or stopped before its end.
It reads the journal in the outputs directory and prints the state of the
directed evolution so far on standard output, without changing it.
It says first that the directed evolution has not ended, and then prints what
\fBcladenc report\fP prints, with the harness that is ahead so far in place of
the best harness.
.PP
Given a directed evolution that has ended, \fBcladenc status\fP prints nothing
on standard output: it says on standard error that the directed evolution has
ended and that \fBcladenc report\fP is the sub-command to call, and exits with
status 2.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Print help.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fP
Print one JSON object in place of the table.
.TP
\fB\-\-outputs\-dir\fP <DIR>
The outputs directory of the directed evolution to print the state of.
.SH THE HARNESS THAT IS AHEAD SO FAR
A directed evolution that has not ended has no best harness.
In its place \fBcladenc status\fP names the harness that is ahead so far: the
harness that would be named the best harness if the directed evolution ended
now.
What \fBcladenc status\fP prints is the state so far, which can change until
the directed evolution ends: another harness can be ahead later, and the lead
of the harness that is ahead so far can grow or shrink.
.PP
\fBcladenc\-report\fP(1) says three things of the best harness and the
primogenitor, counted on the corroboration tasks.
\fBcladenc status\fP says the same three things of the harness that is ahead
so far and the primogenitor.
A person who calls \fBcladenc status\fP many times reads many likelihoods, and
one of many likelihoods is low by luck more often than one that is read once.
Each of them is the state so far, and not the result of the directed
evolution.
.SH EXPERIMENTS
Of the experiments, \fBcladenc status\fP says what \fBcladenc report\fP says,
as \fBcladenc\-report\fP(1) describes.
A corroboration task that the progenitor's child or the singleton control
group harness has not attempted yet is left out.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcladenc\fP(1),
\fBcladenc\-report\fP(1),
\fBcladenc\-resume\fP(1),
\fBcladenc\-start\fP(1)
